pragma solidity ^0.8.24;

/// @notice Interface for a zero-knowledge proof verifier that would allow a
/// rater to prove, without revealing which eligible address they are, that:
///   (a) they hold an active stake- or credential-backed identity, and
///   (b) the rating value they are submitting lies in the valid [1,5] range
///       and corresponds to the committed value being revealed,
/// so that ReputationEngine.revealRatingViaProof() can accept the rating
/// while keeping the rater's address off-chain / unlinkable.
///
/// STATUS NOTE (read this before assuming ZK privacy is implemented):
/// This repository defines ONLY this interface plus a non-cryptographic test
/// double, MockZKVerifier (contracts/mocks/MockZKVerifier.sol), which always
/// returns a hardcoded boolean. No circom circuit, no trusted setup, and no
/// real Groth16/Plonk verifier contract exist in this codebase. Writing and
/// auditing that circuit is substantial additional work tracked in
/// docs/zk-proof-status.md and was explicitly out of scope for this working
/// model. Any production deployment MUST replace MockZKVerifier with a real
/// verifier (e.g. one generated by snarkjs `zkey export solidityverifier`)
/// implementing this same interface.
interface IZKVerifier {
    /// @param proof Opaque proof bytes (circuit-specific encoding).
    /// @param publicSignals Public inputs the circuit exposes (e.g. a
    /// nullifier for the rater, the subject/context hash, and the committed
    /// rating hash). Left as a generic uint256 array since no concrete
    /// circuit has been fixed yet.
    function verifyRatingProof(bytes calldata proof, uint256[] calldata publicSignals) external view returns (bool);
}
